a['summary']=summary;a['conclusions']=['The TM010 near-zero-IF tone response has strong quadrature gain/phase imbalance and image leakage. This is present in raw calibration and independently reproduced in archived FFT power; interpolation is not the primary cause.','A dominant-tone scalar kz is insufficient for a general two-sideband noise prediction when image leakage is large. Including the measured image partially fills the modeled deficit, but leaves most of the discrepancy.','Run680 low-IF noise and short-lag real covariance are stable over five disjoint windows spanning the entire run; this does not establish all possible stationarity properties.','The active scalar toy already overestimates TM010 RMS; an added positive noise term alone cannot simultaneously fix absolute scale and shape at fixed upstream gain/noise.','A coherent-tone transfer calibration does not by itself locate sources of receiver noise. Setup/history and noise-budget reference planes remain needed. ADC ranges and LO settings differ between calibration and science; coupling/filter settings are absent from the saved ODB.','The raw-tone convention is I-jQ. Previous toy spectrum conjugation was unnecessary; fix plot orientation only. Real normalized covariance and modulus are invariant and measured run680 analysis is unchanged.']
